{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"6ce3165b-6548-41f1-977e-72e7ddfccd37","content":"## Build Failure Analysis\n\n**Solution:** `BuildDiag.sln` (3 projects: `Core`, `Services`, `Api`)\n\n**Dependency chain:** `Core` ← `Services` ← `Api`\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause Error (in `Services/UserService.cs`)\n\n| Code | Message |\n|------|---------|\n| **CS0246** | The type or namespace name **'Newtonsoft'** could not be found |\n| **CS0246** | The type or namespace name **'JObject'** could not be found |\n\nThe `Services` project uses `Newtonsoft.Json` (specifically `JObject`) but **does not have a PackageReference** to `Newtonsoft.Json` in `Services.csproj`.\n\n---\n\n### Cascading Failure\n\n| Project | Effect |\n|---------|--------|\n| **Api** | Skipped/failed because its dependency `Services` failed to compile (`Services.dll` does not exist) |\n\n---\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd the missing NuGet package reference to `Services/Services.csproj`:\n\n```xml\n<ItemGroup>\n  <PackageReference Include=\"Newtonsoft.Json\" Version=\"13.0.3\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n```\n\nThis single fix resolves both CS0246 errors in `Services` and unblocks the `Api` project build. The `Core` project compiled successfully on its own.","toolRequests":[],"interactionId":"11e90e11-ad42-4bf1-97d0-055e51e2ea1c","outputTokens":334,"requestId":"E019:3473DA:5CBAF3F:62DC4CD:6A1F80DA"},"id":"3a24caa6-42a4-461e-bb78-5e9f308206b8","timestamp":"2026-06-03T01:18:27.177Z","parentId":"e56ce358-16c9-44d0-8a57-06b97b23e702"}
